  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Language Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating an Arabic/English language toggle into the portfolio. My plan involves using `useState` in `App.tsx` to manage the language state. I\'m exploring the best placement for this toggle on the page to enhance user experience.\n\n\n**Analyzing Translation Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed by focusing on text translation first. I\'ll maintain \"MARWANX\" in English, as suggested, and translate the rest. The key translations are now identified. I\'m prioritizing direct text replacement based on the language state using a simple toggle button, likely in the top-right or top-left corner. I\'m going to look at adding translations for all the text on the page.\n\n\n**Translating Portfolio Content**\n\nI\'m now deep in translating the portfolio\'s content. I\'ve successfully translated phrases such as \"craft it. Shape your reality\" and \"1/26 NEXT PROJECT,\" as well as \"DEVELOPER SKILL\" and \"Visual.\" I also translated \"React 18 NextJS-14,\" \"State,\" \"TS - State Manager,\" \"Motion,\" \"144Hz CSS-Motions,\" \"Build,\" and \"Fullstack Vercel Web-App.\" I\'ve also tackled \"MW-01: SYSTEM CORE,\" and \"High-level React skill and a clean stack for scaling and clarity.\", along with other text.\n\n\n**Implementing Cloud-Ready Translation**\n\nI\'ve translated \"CLOUD-READY\" to \"\330\254\330\247\331\207\330\262 \331\204\331\204\330\263\330\255\330\247\330\250\330\251.\" Now, I\'m focusing on implementation, specifically in `App.tsx` and adding a language toggle. I\'m leaning toward the Top Right Info section for the button. Considering RTL layouts, I\'ve realized `right-8` might be problematic; `end-8` is a better logical property. I\'m exploring setting `dir=\"rtl\"` and adjusting positioning using logical properties or right-aligning Arabic text, as well as testing to determine where `dir=\"rtl\"` should be placed.\n\n\n**Refining RTL Layouts**\n\nI\'m now diving into the complexities of RTL layouts. I\'m considering keeping the page LTR and applying `dir=\"rtl\"` to text containers to preserve the layout. I realized that a full page `dir=\"rtl\"` would flip flex rows.  I\'m exploring how `flex justify-between` will work; it might produce a standard mirrored layout! However, absolute positioning with `right-8` becomes a challenge, potentially overlapping the title. I\'m focusing on using `left-8`, or `end-8`, or Tailwind\'s `ltr:` and `rtl:` variants, or logical properties like `inset-inline-end-8`, and `start-8` to ensure correct positioning regardless of language direction. I\'m researching these variants to determine the best approach.\n\n\n**Adapting Property Usage**\n\nI\'m now adapting the project to use logical properties, replacing physical ones. I\'m swapping `right-8` with `end-8`, `md:right-16` with `md:end-16`, `border-r` with `border-e`, `text-left` with `text-start`, and `text-right` with `text-end`. I\'m also looking into `App.tsx` and creating a content dictionary for efficient translation management, as shown above, to organize English text.\n\n\n**Implementing New Translations**\n\nI\'ve added translations for \"Hire Marwan\" (\"\331\210\330\270\331\201 \331\205\330\261\331\210\330\247\331\206\"), \"FULL-STACK\" (\"\331\205\330\252\331\203\330\247\331\205\331\204\") and \"CLOUD-READY\" (\"\330\254\330\247\331\207\330\262 \331\204\331\204\330\263\330\255\330\247\330\250\330\251\"), as well as various content and titles. I\'ve focused on keeping the translation process smooth and efficient by implementing a content dictionary for easy management. I\'m now making adjustments to the portfolio content.\n\n\n**Adjusting Font Integration**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the font strategy for Arabic support. I\'m importing \'Cairo\', \'Tajawal\', or \'IBM Plex Sans Arabic\' from Google Fonts and will incorporate one of them into the project. I\'m aiming to avoid any font-related display issues and maintain font consistency between English and Arabic characters. I\'m focusing on ensuring proper font integration for improved text presentation based on language direction.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 18
      nanos: 977139677
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
